  "worked_solution": "We know that any vector in  $\\text{Span}{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ has the form\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -\\frac{8}{3} \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 18\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the coordinates relative to the basis $\\,B.$ Since we are told that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],$ we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={{(\\frac{3}{2})}_{\u23df}}_{{x}_{1}}[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -\\frac{8}{3} \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}]+{{(-3)}_{\u23df}}_{{x}_{2}}[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 18\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 18\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-18 \\\\ -30 \\\\ -54\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ -34 \\\\ -36\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
